.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt MAVERGREEN-FLEET 1
.Os Mavergreen
.Sh NAME
.Nm mavergreen-fleet
.Nd what needs a human across the Mavergreen family, and retries for transient failures
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -help
.Nm
.Cm attention
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm remediate
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm timing
.Op Fl -since Ar when
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -json
.Op Ar repo Op Ar run-id
.Nm
.Cm graph
.Op Fl -dot | Fl -mermaid | Fl -json
.Op Fl -from-dir Ar dir
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the Mavergreen GitHub organization's public repositories and reports on them.
It needs a token that can read the organization; see
.Sx ENVIRONMENT .
.Pp
Text output uses colour, and is cut to the terminal's width (or
.Ev COLUMNS ) ,
only on a terminal.
Piped, it is never truncated.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm attention
Lists what needs a human, most urgent first: stuck pull requests, red workflows,
issues waiting for a reply, retries in progress, and anything it could not read.
Each finding ends with what to do about it.
An empty list still says what was checked.
.It Cm remediate Op Fl -dry-run
Retries failures that match a known transient pattern, at most twice each.
For a Renovate pull request it ticks the rebase/retry checkbox, so Renovate rebuilds the branch.
For a run on
.Ql main ,
or a scheduled run, it re-runs the failed jobs.
Every other failure is reported, not retried.
It never merges, cancels or deletes anything.
.Fl -dry-run
says what it would do and changes nothing.
.It Cm timing Op Ar repo Op Ar run-id
Where Actions time goes.
With no
.Ar repo ,
a table per repo and runner kind (macOS or Linux): queue wait, run time, re-runs and wasted hours.
With a
.Ar repo ,
Gantt bars of queue wait and run time for that repo's latest
.Pa release.yml
run, or for
.Ar run-id .
.Pp
Each run not yet cached costs one GitHub API request from the hourly quota every agent shares.
A fleet-wide run that would leave fewer than 500 requests this hour stops and says so.
.It Cm graph
The family's ingredient graph: its edges, diamonds and cycles, plus what it could not read.
How long a change takes to flow along it is not shown yet.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -help , Fl h
With no command, or as
.Cm help ,
list the commands.
After a command, print that command's usage.
.Nm
alone does the same as
.Fl -help .
.It Fl -json
Print one JSON object on stdout instead of text; see
.Sx JSON OUTPUT .
.It Fl -dry-run
.Cm remediate
only: change nothing.
.It Fl -since Ar when
.Cm timing
only: the start of the window, as a date
.Pq Ql 2026-11-01
or a duration back from now
.Po
.Ql 7d ,
.Ql 48h
.Pc .
Default:
.Ql 7d .
.It Fl -force
.Cm timing
only: run even when the quota check would stop it.
.It Fl -dot , Fl -mermaid
.Cm graph
only: print the graph in that format.
.It Fl -from-dir Ar dir
.Cm graph
only: read a directory of family checkouts instead of the organization.
.It Fl -version
Print
.Ql mavergreen-fleet VERSION .
.El
.Sh JSON OUTPUT
Every command prints one object, never truncated or coloured.
Lists are
.Ql []
when empty, never
.Ql null .
Every object starts with:
.Bl -tag -width generated
.It Li schema
.Ql \(dqfleet/v1\(dq .
.It Li command
.Ql attention ,
.Ql remediate ,
.Ql timing
or
.Ql graph .
.It Li generated
When it ran, RFC 3339 in UTC, such as
.Ql 2026-11-19T12:00:00Z .
.El
.Pp
The command's own fields follow.
.Ss attention
.Bl -tag -width findings
.It Li checked
.Li {repos, prs, issues, runs} ,
counts of what was read.
.It Li findings
.Li {repo, item, url, kind, since, why, fix} ,
most urgent first.
.Li kind
is
.Ql cannot-read ,
.Ql stuck-pr ,
.Ql red-workflow ,
.Ql needs-reply
or
.Ql retry-in-progress .
.Li item
is
.Ql repo#123
for a pull request or issue and
.Ql repo:workflow
for a workflow; for
.Ql cannot-read
it names what could not be read (an API path, or
.Dq checks for repo#123 ) ,
and
.Li why
carries the error.
.Li since
is RFC 3339.
.El
.Ss remediate
.Bl -tag -width actions
.It Li actions
.Li {kind, repo, pr, run_id, run_url, pattern, attempt, note, done, dry_run, error} .
.Li kind
is
.Ql tick-box ,
.Ql rerun
or
.Ql report .
An action declined at the last moment comes back as a
.Ql report ,
and so does something that could not be read, with
.Li error
saying why.
.Li pr ,
.Li run_id ,
.Li run_url ,
.Li pattern ,
.Li attempt
and
.Li error
are left out when they do not apply.
.Li done
is true only when the write happened.
.El
.Ss timing, with no repo
.Bl -tag -width unreadable_runs
.It Li window_start
The first day counted,
.Ql YYYY-MM-DD .
.It Li repos
One row per repo and runner kind, most total hours first:
.Li {repo, kind, jobs, wait_h, median_wait_m, p90_wait_m, run_h, never_started, never_started_wait_h, reruns, manual_kicks, wasted_h, total_h} .
.Li kind
is
.Ql macos
or
.Ql linux .
Unfinished jobs are not counted.
.It Li unreadable_runs
.Li {<repo>: <runs whose jobs could not be read>} .
Those runs are left out of
.Li repos .
.It Li cannot_read
One line per thing that could not be read (a repo's run list, a run's jobs).
.El
.Ss timing repo Op run-id
.Bl -tag -width critical_path
.It Li repo , Li run_id
.Li run_id
is absent when the repo has no runs.
.It Li note
When there is something to say: no
.Pa release.yml
run, so another workflow's; or no runs at all.
.It Li jobs
.Li {name, attempt, labels, created, started, completed, wait_s, run_s, never_started, conclusion} ,
every attempt's jobs.
.It Li critical_path
Job names, earliest first.
.El
.Pp
A repo or run that cannot be read is exit 1, not a field.
.Ss graph
.Bl -tag -width incomplete
.It Li edges
.Li {consumer, ingredient} .
.It Li diamonds , Li cycles
The
.Ql DIAMOND
and
.Ql CYCLE
lines of shipyard's
.Pa family-graph.sh .
.It Li incomplete
Repos it skipped and names it could not map
.Ql ( SKIP ... ,
.Ql UNMAPPED ... ) .
.It Li timings
Says propagation timings are not yet available.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width SHIPYARD_SCRIPTS
.It Ev GH_TOKEN
The token, when set; otherwise what
.Ql gh auth token
prints.
.It Ev SHIPYARD_SCRIPTS
Where shipyard's scripts are, for
.Cm graph
and for repos' declared deviations.
Default:
.Pa /usr/local/mavergreen/shipyard/share/cmake/MavericksShipyard/scripts .
.It Ev COLUMNS
The width to cut text to, on a terminal.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
It printed its report.
Something it could not read does not change this; a script must check
.Cm attention Ns 's
.Ql cannot-read
findings,
.Cm remediate Ns 's
.Li error ,
.Cm timing Ns 's
.Li cannot_read
and
.Li unreadable_runs ,
or
.Cm graph Ns 's
.Li incomplete .
.It 1
An error.
Any command: no token; the organization's repos or the token's user could not be read; output could not be written.
.Cm remediate :
a write failed, or a read it needed just before writing failed (something unread while planning is a report, exit 0).
.Cm timing :
the repo or run asked for cannot be read; the quota check stopped it; or, as text only, it read no runs and something could not be read.
.Cm graph :
.Pa family-graph.sh
exited with anything but 0 or 3 (3 is a partial graph), or the shipyard scripts are missing.
.It 2
A usage error: an unknown command or argument, a bad
.Fl -since
or run id.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
See what needs attention:
.Dl $ mavergreen-fleet attention
.Pp
See what remediate would retry, then retry it:
.Dl $ mavergreen-fleet remediate --dry-run
.Dl $ mavergreen-fleet remediate
.Pp
Where ed25519's latest release run spent its time:
.Dl $ mavergreen-fleet timing ed25519
.Pp
Draw the family graph:
.Dl $ mavergreen-fleet graph --dot | dot -Tsvg > family.svg
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gh 1
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/Mavergreen/fleet
